gfs2: Rename LM_FLAG_{NOEXP -> RECOVER}

jira KERNEL-1773
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10
commit-author Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
commit 1714e8543dbe21bbd33e62df926552f943f8f5cd
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10/1714e854.failed

GFS sets the LM_FLAG_NOEXP flag on locking requests it makes during
journal recovery, so rename the flag to LM_FLAG_RECOVER for improved
code readability.

	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1714e8543dbe21bbd33e62df926552f943f8f5cd)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/gfs2/ops_fstype.c
#	fs/gfs2/super.c
#	fs/gfs2/util.c
